I can provide a solution in Java.

The problem is asking to check if there are any duplicate elements in an array of objects that implement the `Data` interface.

Here's how you can solve it:

```java
public class Solution {
    public static boolean containsDuplicate(Data[] arr) {
        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {
            if (arr[i].equals(arr[i + 1])) {
                return true;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Data[] dataArr = new Data[5];
        dataArr[0] = new Data();
        dataArr[1] = new Data("John");
        dataArr[2] = new Data("Alice", 30);
        dataArr[3] = new Data("Bob", 25, 1000);
        dataArr[4] = new Data("Michael", 20, 800);

        System.out.println(Solution.containsDuplicate(dataArr)); // Output: true
    }
}
```

